// @reject: a pattern that names an error's message stands alone in its arm:
// @reject: `m` would not exist when the other alternative matched. `##A(_) ||
// @reject: ##B` is fine. Decided with the pattern, 2026-09-29 (D7, GAP-GOL-016).
r = ##A("x")
?? r {
    ##A(m) || ##B(m) => { >> m ¶ }
    _                => { >> "o" ¶ }
}
